COMMITMENTS
  whosaid commitments <ws> [--owner NAME|me] [--all-owners] [--json] [-o FILE]
  "What did I sign up for, across every meeting, ranked": a view over the
  roll-up corpora (_commitments.json + _action-items.json), never a store.
  Items are the owner's CM-NNN commitments plus the AI-NNN action items they
  own (name match; '_' and ' ' interchangeable; [workspace] aliases too); an
  action item that reads like one of the commitments folds into that line as
  "(also AI-NNN)". Tiers, deterministic and LLM-free:
    P1  boss-requested, a blocking/urgency cue (urgent, outage, prod issue,
        customer escalation, ...), a deadline cue (tomorrow, eod, by friday,
        2026-09-30, ...), or seen in 3+ meetings
    P2  seen in 2 meetings, requested by anyone, or a strong cue ("I'll own",
        "I will", "I promise") in the latest meeting
    P3  everything else; negated items ("I won't") are never P1
  A cue right after a negator in the same clause (non-urgent, not blocking,
  no rush) does not count. A relative deadline (today, tomorrow, this week,
  by friday) resolves against the meeting it was said in; once that date is
  behind today the line says overdue=YYYY-MM-DD instead of due=..., the
  small overdue weight replaces deadline, and the item is no longer P1 on
  the deadline alone (WHOSAID_TODAY=YYYY-MM-DD pins today).
  Within a tier: score, then most recent, then id. whosaid.toml [commitments]
  overrides the lists and weights: boss = [...], deadline_cues, blocking_cues,
  negators, strong_cues, weak_cues, weights.{boss,blocking,deadline,overdue,
  repeat,recent,strong,requested,negative}, embed_threshold. Roll-up writes
  the same view to <ws>/_WORKLIST-<Owner>.md; ids never renumber; edit
  _COMMITMENTS.md or _ACTION-ITEMS.md, not the worklist.
  --owner NAME|me     A speaker label, or me (default): the 'self'-roled
                      speaker, else [workspace] owner.
  --all-owners        Every participant (markdown concatenated; --json wraps
                      them as {"owners": [...]}).
  --json              {owner, generated_from, items: [{id, source, text, status,
                      tier, score, why, first_seen, last_seen, occurrences,
                      requested_by, negative, also}]}.
  -o, --out FILE      Write there instead of stdout.

WORKSPACE SEARCH
  <ws> is the meeting workspace directory. Every search command also accepts it
  from $WHOSAID_WORKSPACE, or from the current directory when that holds
  _workspace.json or whosaid.toml, so <ws> may be omitted.

  index      Builds <ws>/_search.db: an FTS5 table over every *.speakers.txt
             (dated or hand-named folders alike), optional neural embeddings via
             Ollama nomic-embed-text on 127.0.0.1 (skipped with --no-embed or
             when Ollama is down; exact search still works), and the entity
             tables (person, meeting, action_item, occurrence, commitment,
             pr_mention) derived from the manifest, the action-item corpus, each
             meeting's action-items.md, and the transcripts. Then writes
             <ws>/_WIKI.md. Steps run in order: search, graph, wiki; the first
             failure stops the run and is named. --rebuild drops and recreates
             the database; the file is always safe to delete.
  search     --mode exact (FTS5: words, "phrases", AND/OR/NOT; the default),
             meaning (nearest embeddings), or hybrid (both, fused). meaning and
             hybrid fall back to exact when Ollama is down. --speaker and --meeting
             narrow the hits, -k caps them, --json prints one object per hit.
             Each hit prints "[meeting @ HH:MM:SS] Speaker: ...snippet...".
  context    The verbatim turns --before (default 60 s) and --after (default
             120 s) a timestamp in one meeting, for reading a hit in place.
  graph      items [--owner N] [--requester N] [--status S] [--type T]
             item AI-NNN (detail, occurrences, timestamped commitments)
             person [Name] (talk share, commitments they made and asked for)
             prs (PR numbers mentioned, spoken or written) | meetings (coverage)
             speakers (talk share per speaker across the workspace)
  wiki       Regenerates <ws>/_WIKI.md from the graph; --stdout prints instead.
  Per-workspace settings live in <ws>/whosaid.toml (owner, groups, summarizer,
  search, watch); see the README for the full example.

WATCH
  whosaid watch install --into <ws> [--source DIR] [--seed] [--dry-run]
                        [--interpreter PATH] [--label L] [--interval S]
                        [--offline] [--env K=V ...] [--no-open] [--no-fda]
  whosaid watch run     --into <ws> [--source DIR] [--seed] [--dry-run]
                        [--accurate] [--offline] [--whosaid PATH] [--engine E]
  whosaid watch uninstall [--into <ws> | --label L] [--purge]
  whosaid watch status    [--into <ws> | --label L] [--json]
  install writes a launchd LaunchAgent that watches --source (default: the macOS
  Voice Memos store) and, once a recording's mtime has been stable, stages it
  out of the TCC-protected store and runs 'whosaid ingest --action-items
  --commitments', then roll-up and index. --seed marks the recordings already there as done. Full
  Disk Access is granted to ONE dedicated, ad-hoc-signed interpreter the
  installer provisions; --interpreter PATH reuses a binary you already granted.
  --source works for any folder, not just Voice Memos. --no-fda defaults an
  unset source to ~/Recordings: the FDA toggle needs an admin password (see
  README 'No admin rights?'). uninstall --purge also
  removes the interpreter, state file, and log. run is the same pipeline in the
  foreground (--dry-run lists what would be ingested).

  whosaid memos list [--source DIR] [--json]     Titles and sync state.
  whosaid memos pull [--latest | --title T] [-o DIR]
                                                 Copy a memo out of the store.
  whosaid memos delete "<title>" [--yes]         Delete through the Voice Memos
                                                 app's own Delete Recordings
                                                 intent (a one-action Shortcut),
                                                 never the files or database.
  whosaid memos shortcut-recipe                  How to build that Shortcut.

ENV OVERRIDES
  WHOSAID_MODEL        Default Whisper model repo.
  WHOSAID_LANG         Default language code.
  WHOSAID_VOICE_REFS   Directory of enrollment clips (default: ./voices).
  WHOSAID_SPEAKER_DB   Local speaker registry (default: ~/.config/whosaid/speakers.json).
  WHOSAID_ABSORB_THRESHOLD  Absorb-pass cosine threshold (default: 0.85); a still-
                      unnamed cluster this close to a known voice is folded into it.
  WHOSAID_MATCH_THRESHOLD  Registry/reference match cosine threshold (default: 0.50);
                      a cluster whose best candidate scores below it stays SPEAKER_NN.
  DIARIZE_EMB_NAME     Speaker-embedding model (default: NeMo TitaNet-small,
                       English-native; set the zh-cn model for Mandarin audio).
  WHOSAID_REC_DEVICE   avfoundation audio device index (default: 0).
  WHOSAID_INSTALL_DIR  Command install directory (default: ~/.local/bin).
  WHOSAID_ACTION_ITEMS_HOOK  Default action-items summarizer hook: gets the
                      transcript on stdin, prints markdown on stdout, and reads
                      WHOSAID_TRANSCRIPT_PATH, WHOSAID_SPEAKERS, WHOSAID_ROLES.
  WHOSAID_WORKSPACE    Default meeting workspace for index/search/context/graph/
                      wiki, for 'whosaid doctor', and for the read-only search
                      tools of 'whosaid mcp'.
  WHOSAID_OWNER        Whose action items a workspace tracks (overrides
                      whosaid.toml [workspace] owner).
  WHOSAID_TODAY        YYYY-MM-DD the worklist treats as today when deciding
                      whether a relative deadline is overdue (default: the
                      clock).
  WHOSAID_OLLAMA       Ollama base URL for embeddings and the built-in summarizer
                      (default: http://127.0.0.1:11434; localhost only).
  WHOSAID_SUMMARIZER_MODEL  Ollama model for the built-in action-items engine
                      (default: qwen2.5:14b).
  WHOSAID_BIN          The whosaid command the watcher runs (default: this script).
  HF_HOME               Hugging Face cache location (Whisper model cache).
  SHERPA_DIARIZE_CACHE  sherpa-onnx diarization model cache location.

Diarization writes <base>.rttm and merges with the Whisper output into
<base>.speakers.txt (the speaker-labeled transcript). Diarization failure never
loses the plain transcript — it warns and the transcript stands on its own.

Nothing — audio, text, or embeddings — ever leaves the machine.
EOF
}

